  "about": "Ground truth from Wael's screenshots of each mosque's own site. `node scout.mjs --check` reads each site in a real browser (or re-reads a screenshot fixture, writing nothing) and compares Claude's extraction with these keys. Times are iqama, 24-hour, Toronto. Rules: \"sunset\", \"sunset+3\", \"adhan+5\". A key is compared only on dates inside valid_from..valid_to; an expired key is a warning. `rules` lists the rulebook ids (supabase/functions/scout/rules.ts) the key exercises; the check reports every rule as passing, failing or untested. When a key and the live site disagree, first check the site's primary data (feed, widget, image): if the mosque changed its times, end the old key and add a new one; only a disagreement with the primary data is a Scout bug. \"expect\": \"held back\" = adhan-only page (passes only if nothing is stored as iqama); \"expect\": \"bot check\" = the site refuses automated readers (passes when the refusal is recognised). Keys with \"image\" are screenshot fixtures (screenshot inbox), read with the same rules.",
